"version of this interval, drawn at the large-sample radius mada uses (2.45 "
"at 95%), while this interval uses t on k-2 df. They therefore do not "
"coincide: below about eight studies the printed interval is the wider of the "
"two, and above that the region is. Read them as two views of the same "
"quantity rather than matching one to the other."
msgstr ""

